From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36b64d56-bf1c-11f1-acdf-6701c49d00b5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:35:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Lula and Bolsonaro tied in polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls</link><description>
Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Mara Nogueira, Senior Lecturer in Urban Geography at Birbeck, University of London, says the tight race reflects the consolidation of two political camps, with many Brazilians voting not out of support for a candidate, but to keep the other out of power. She points to the cost of living, religion and social media echo chambers as key factors shaping the vote, alongside a major banking scandal that has so far had limited impact on Flavio Bolsonaro’s campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/148e8480-bff5-11f1-baa5-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-140634-141113-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/148e8480-bff5-11f1-baa5-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-140634-141113-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">192b2bba-bff5-11f1-a72c-d5f3666ace29</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:19:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula de Silva: 80-year-old incumbent Brazilian president seeks 4th term</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term</link><description>
Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko tells us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a972198-bff4-11f1-ad27-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-140151-140634-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a972198-bff4-11f1-ad27-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-140151-140634-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f88d7e6-bff4-11f1-a9b2-3f124670dd82</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:17:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's leader announces counter-offensive as Houthis cut off supply route to besieged city</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz</link><description>
The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00fb47e-bfee-11f1-9c60-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9E87YK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00fb47e-bfee-11f1-9c60-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9E87YK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f53ebc8-bff1-11f1-91cc-b955e607a27f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:59:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d00fb47e-bfee-11f1-9c60-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C9E87YK.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Up to 500 French schools to be totally or partly closed Monday amid student protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261004-up-to-500-french-schools-to-be-totally-or-partly-closed-monday-due-to-protests</link><description>
Lessons will be "totally or partly suspended" at up to 500 high schools across France on Monday, the country's education minister has said, after days of sometimes violent protests against teacher shortages, dilapidated school buildings and overcrowding in classrooms. The minister said 24 schools had been "burned or ransacked" since the start of protests.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d80878-be43-11f1-b4ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/022ba4e8b312d3db20028d7ab7851a66d3b76f5e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d80878-be43-11f1-b4ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/022ba4e8b312d3db20028d7ab7851a66d3b76f5e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37553b92-bff2-11f1-b376-237bf166e242</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:50:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d80878-be43-11f1-b4ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/022ba4e8b312d3db20028d7ab7851a66d3b76f5e.jpg">© Fred Tanneau, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rwandan genocide suspect 'hunter' Dafroza Gauthier dies at 72</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261004-rwandan-genocide-hunter-dafroza-gauthier-dies-at-72</link><description>
For nearly 30 years, Dafroza Gauthier, along with her husband Alain, tracked down Rwandan refugees in France suspected of having participated in the Tutsi genocide. She died in Reims on Saturday after dedicating her life to bringing to justice those allegedly responsible for the 1994 massacre of more than 800,000 people. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59ce40b6-bfd8-11f1-82be-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23327396671319.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59ce40b6-bfd8-11f1-82be-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23327396671319.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a37d0da2-bfea-11f1-8923-bb89061cdae9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:12:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59ce40b6-bfd8-11f1-82be-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23327396671319.jpg">© Christophe Ena, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones</link><description>
Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72da03b6-be74-11f1-bf6c-41e1b8a52073</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:01:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png">© The Observers / Herd of Justice</source><dc:creator>Marguerite Ipek LACROIX</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula and Bolsonaro face off in Brazil presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race</link><description>
Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the presidential race is centred on two rivals: President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator. Dr Andrea Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King's College Brazil Institute in London, shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4af16eb0-bfe7-11f1-a8ca-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-130852-131819-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4af16eb0-bfe7-11f1-a8ca-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-130852-131819-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5019f81c-bfe7-11f1-a747-936a5daf9f74</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 11:56:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Cornell president breaks silence over alleged campus rape</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape</link><description>
Cornell University remains at the centre of controversy over an alleged gang rape at a fraternity on campus, with the university president now breaking his silence. In an eight-minute video statement released Saturday night, Michael Kotlikoff called the allegations, made by a woman known as Jane Doe, deeply disturbing and said the university must do better. Shirli Sitbon has this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22935d1c-bfe6-11f1-95ff-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-130412-130611-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22935d1c-bfe6-11f1-95ff-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-130412-130611-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27ab91a2-bfe6-11f1-894f-1dfb2b076328</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 11:53:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil heads to the polls for high-stakes election between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e99df506-bff1-11f1-b070-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D27G68K.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e99df506-bff1-11f1-b070-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D27G68K.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39db38ba-bfe5-11f1-976b-199a82b6f5af</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 11:17:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e99df506-bff1-11f1-b070-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D27G68K.jpg">© Sergio Lima, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7</link><description>
An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99316d34-bfe0-11f1-8d20-8fa7ddd26abe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 10:59:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian strike hits Kyiv amid Chancellor Merz visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strike-hits-kyiv-amid-chancellor-merz-visit</link><description>
Moscow has once again bombed one of Kyiv’s bridges, despite the presence of German Chancellor Friedrich Merz in the Ukrainian capital. The visit was unplanned, but Merz says it was intended to show Germany’s support for Ukraine. France 24 correspondent Gulliver Cragg, reporting from Kyiv, says traffic has resumed on the bridge, though slowly. Video shows a large hole in the roadway. Experts say the bridges are extremely solid and difficult to destroy, even with ballistic missiles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e390ed6c-bfd8-11f1-82ff-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-110613-111023-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e390ed6c-bfd8-11f1-82ff-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-110613-111023-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e851ca60-bfd8-11f1-ab83-5fde8dfa6e76</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:52:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: A portrait of Flavio Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-a-portrait-of-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
Brazilians are voting for governors and lawmakers, but the biggest stakes are in the presidential race. Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the contest is seen as a toss-up between President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6f86b4a-bfd7-11f1-914f-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-110148-110322-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6f86b4a-bfd7-11f1-914f-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-110148-110322-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb7ede7e-bfd7-11f1-bb56-257e158da7e1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:49:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Who are the mystery pilots who successfully landed endangered Flydubai flight 1073?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073</link><description>
A passenger on Flydubai flight 1073 has described the actions of on-duty crew members who rushed into the cockpit to stabilise and land the plane after the co-pilot attacked the captain with a crash axe. The flight carrying 182 people en route to Israel Wednesday was able to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8218d5c8-bfcd-11f1-a3ed-df9ae4e03873</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:36:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tsar Samuel laid to rest in Sofia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tsar-samuel-laid-to-rest-in-sofia</link><description>
In Bulgaria, the remains of medieval ruler Tsar Samuel have been laid to rest in the capital Sofia, after being flown back from the border with Greece by Bulgarian fighter jets. Their return follows decades of negotiations with Athens, in exchange for the return of religious artefacts. Nicholas Rushworth has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e04ee4e2-bfce-11f1-9ded-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-101231-101417-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e04ee4e2-bfce-11f1-9ded-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-101231-101417-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e512f18a-bfce-11f1-92d1-a1bfcac55e03</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:40:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ireland–Israel nations League clash overshadowed by political tensions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261004-ireland%E2%80%93israel-nations-league-clash-overshadowed-by-political-tensions</link><description>
Ireland and Israel are set to face off in the second leg of their Nations League matchup, with political tensions overshadowing the football. During last week’s first game in Bulgaria, Irish players wore black armbands in support of Gaza and pointedly lowered their heads during the Israeli national anthem. Ahead of Sunday’s match in Serbia, the Irish team cut a press conference short after facing intense questioning from Israeli journalists. Charlotte Lam has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/093dd44c-bfcc-11f1-a22f-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-095127-095332-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/093dd44c-bfcc-11f1-a22f-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-095127-095332-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e686df6-bfcc-11f1-b455-7b849efc4829</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:27:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil polls open in a few hours</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-polls-open-in-a-few-hours</link><description>
Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his main challenger Flavio Bolsonaro wrapped up their campaigns on Saturday in the powerhouse state of Sao Paulo, where a fifth of the nation's vote is based, seeking to rally supporters and convince the undecided on the eve of Sunday's nail-biter election. Mareeke Reethof, lecturer in Latin American Politics at the University of Liverpool, shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2d762a2-bfcb-11f1-8523-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090829-091808-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2d762a2-bfcb-11f1-8523-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090829-091808-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7c929ee-bfcb-11f1-8f07-3d6ebccde61b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:25:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Flock's AI tracking sparks privacy fears and violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/flock-s-ai-tracking-sparks-privacy-fears-and-violence</link><description>
In the US, Flock Security cameras form an AI-powered surveillance network that records licence plates and other vehicle information. Their controversial use has become a political issue ahead of the midterm elections, and the cameras are increasingly being targeted by vandals. Caitlin Brown explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bdbd99c-bfcc-11f1-bd77-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-095423-095630-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bdbd99c-bfcc-11f1-bd77-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-095423-095630-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60ad241c-bfcc-11f1-a5fd-57b3c23b77bb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:23:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen’s Houthis claim attacks on Aramco facilities in Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh</link><description>
Yemen’s Houthi rebels have claimed responsibility for attacks in Riyadh, including on facilities belonging to Aramco, the world’s largest oil company. This follows reports from residents of flames and smoke rising from an oil facility on the outskirts of the Saudi capital. Meanwhile, the Houthis have accused Saudi Arabia of launching dozens of strikes on Sanaa, warning that they will continue to respond to any escalation with further escalation. Here’s Jennie Shin with more on the situation on the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f759acd4-bfca-11f1-b895-5fa848c9c018</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:21:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian cities</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-cities</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz arrived in Ukraine's capital Kyiv on Sunday on an unannounced visit in a show of support for the country in its war with Russia. Merz's visit comes just a day after Russia warned foreigners and diplomats to leave the Ukrainian capital, saying that "massive" new airstrikes would hit the city. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Gulliver Cragg has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b6692c-bfc8-11f1-bdda-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-093117-093546-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b6692c-bfc8-11f1-bdda-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-093117-093546-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98181082-bfc8-11f1-87e1-57b3c23b77bb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 07:58:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: New Russian strikes hit Kyiv bridge as Germany's Merz visits</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-live-germany-s-merz-in-kyiv-for-talks-with-zelensky</link><description>
Kyiv’s North bridge was hit in a new Russian attack on Sunday, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said, soon after German Chancellor Friedrich Merz arrived in Ukraine's capital. Merz is on a surprise visit to demonstrate European support in the face of an upsurge in Russian attacks on Ukrainian infrastructure. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f62f0f32-bfc2-11f1-94c5-21597aa5b1df</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 07:28:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Ossoff and El-Sayed: Two Senate races and what they say about the Democratic Party</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-ossoff-and-el-sayed-two-senate-races-and-what-they-say-about-the-democratic-party</link><description>
Senator Jon Ossoff, a Democratic favourite, is running for re-election in Georgia in the 2026 US midterms while Abdul El-Sayed is a Senate candidate in the battleground state of Michigan. The two Democrats have very different profiles and platforms, underscoring divergences within the party. They could also determine the party's future ahead of the 2028 presidential election. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64a85de8-bcd4-11f1-9439-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/main-ossof-sayed.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64a85de8-bcd4-11f1-9439-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/main-ossof-sayed.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1ef0102-bcd4-11f1-a8da-8f92b66c42e9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 07:21:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/64a85de8-bcd4-11f1-9439-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/main-ossof-sayed.png">© Graphic studio FMM (composite)</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bosnia votes in general election with wartime divisions still dominating</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bosnia-votes-in-general-election-with-wartime-divisions-still-dominating</link><description>
Bosnia is heading to the polls on Sunday after a general election campaign dominated by parties that identify closely with the ethnic divisions of its 1990s war. Voters will elect a vast number of officials across multiple tiers of government, in a complex system that has held the partitioned country together since the 1995 peace deal. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Belgrade Laurent Rouy has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2691dfe8-bfbd-11f1-9fa4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-081237-081823-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2691dfe8-bfbd-11f1-9fa4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-081237-081823-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bb8a006-bfbd-11f1-b334-810f6be85510</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 06:51:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Bosnians vote as pro-Russian politician looms large and ethnic tensions simmer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-polls-open-in-bosnia-and-herzegovina-as-pro-russian-politician-looms-large-over-race</link><description>
Bosnians head to the polls Sunday in elections that ​could impact how much influence Russia has over the small Balkan nation, with separatist Serb leader Milorad Dodik dominating the campaign despite his ban from public office. Bosnia and Herzegovina, a country marred by ethnic tensions, has struggled to recover since its brutal 1992-95 conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f34530f6-bfb5-11f1-be74-f9987177d2cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 05:55:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg">© Armin Durgut, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
